Materials is released as open-source software, open educational
resources, public-domain material, or under any permissive,
copyleft, Creative Commons, MIT, Apache, BSD, or similar public license.

Public accessibility of a repository, file, document, demonstration,
website, or generated artifact does not constitute a grant of rights
to reproduce, modify, redistribute, commercialize, sublicense,
or create derivative works from the Materials.


3. COVERED MATERIALS

For purposes of this License, "Materials" includes, without limitation:

(a) curriculum architectures and course structures;

(b) Broad Study Direction (BSD) models and related academic mappings;

(c) academic field, knowledge-stem, cognition-space, and other
    knowledge-structure models;

(d) syllabi, learning objectives, instructional sequences,
    slide structures, assignments, projects, rubrics, and
    educational artifacts;

(e) curriculum-generation workflows, transformation models,
    reasoning procedures, semantic-state models, and related
    methodological materials;

(f) Human-AI collaborative workflows and methods developed
    in connection with RXI-Lab;

(g) JSON, YAML, schemas, configuration files, structured datasets,
    and intermediate semantic states;

(h) source code, scripts, software components, renderers,
    prototypes, interfaces, and Workbench implementations;

(i) diagrams, documentation, research notes, specifications,
    visual materials, and design artifacts; and

(j) derivative or substantially similar implementations based upon
    protected expression contained in the foregoing Materials.


